{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Security Hardening Validator",
  "description": "REQ-45, REQ-46, REQ-51: Security vulnerability detection - SQL injection, XSS, CSRF, API security, rate limiting, input validation",
  "version": "1.1",
  "priority": "critical",
  "model": "claude-opus-4.5",
  "exitCodes": {
    "blocking": [2],
    "warning": [1],
    "success": [0]
  },
  "timeout": 30000,

  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "backend/api/**/*.py",
      "backend/core/auth_middleware.py",
      "backend/core/csrf_protection.py",
      "backend/core/rate_limiting.py",
      "backend/core/input_validation.py",
      "backend/database/**/*.py",
      "backend/services/**/*_service.py",
      "frontend/src/api.ts",
      "frontend/src/utils/validation.ts",
      "frontend/src/hooks/useAuth.ts"
    ]
  },

  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "CRITICAL SECURITY HARDENING VALIDATION:\n\n1. **SQL Injection Protection** (REQ-45.1):\n   ❌ REJECT: Raw SQL queries with string concatenation\n   ❌ REJECT: f-strings or % formatting in SQL queries\n   ✅ REQUIRE: SQLAlchemy ORM or parameterized queries only\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Input validation before database queries\n   \n   Example violations:\n   ```python\n   # BAD - SQL Injection risk\n   query = f\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '{email}'\"\n   \n   # GOOD - Parameterized\n   query = session.query(User).filter(User.email == email)\n   ```\n\n2. **XSS Protection** (REQ-45.2):\n   ❌ REJECT: innerHTML without sanitization\n   ❌ REJECT: dangerouslySetInnerHTML in React\n   ❌ REJECT: eval() or Function() constructor\n   ✅ REQUIRE: DOMPurify for HTML sanitization\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Content Security Policy headers\n   \n   Example violations:\n   ```typescript\n   // BAD - XSS risk\n   element.innerHTML = userInput;\n   \n   // GOOD - Sanitized\n   element.innerHTML = DOMPurify.sanitize(userInput);\n   ```\n\n3. **CSRF Protection** (REQ-45.3):\n   ❌ REJECT: POST/PUT/DELETE endpoints without CSRF token\n   ✅ REQUIRE: CSRF token validation for state-changing operations\n   ✅ REQUIRE: SameSite=Strict cookie attribute\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Double-submit cookie pattern or synchronizer token\n   \n   Example violations:\n   ```python\n   # BAD - No CSRF protection\n   @router.post(\"/api/users\")\n   async def create_user(data: UserCreate):\n       ...\n   \n   # GOOD - CSRF protected\n   @router.post(\"/api/users\")\n   @csrf_protect\n   async def create_user(data: UserCreate, csrf_token: str = Header(...)):\n       ...\n   ```\n\n4. **Authentication & Authorization** (REQ-45.4):\n   ❌ REJECT: Endpoints without authentication\n   ❌ REJECT: Missing role-based access control (RBAC)\n   ❌ REJECT: JWT tokens without expiry (max 1 hour)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: JWT verification on all protected endpoints\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Role checks (student/teacher/parent/admin)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Session timeout (15 min inactivity)\n   \n   Example violations:\n   ```python\n   # BAD - No auth check\n   @router.get(\"/api/students/{id}/grades\")\n   async def get_grades(id: int):\n       ...\n   \n   # GOOD - Auth + RBAC\n   @router.get(\"/api/students/{id}/grades\")\n   async def get_grades(id: int, user: User = Depends(get_current_user)):\n       if user.role not in [\"student\", \"teacher\", \"parent\"]:\n           raise HTTPException(403)\n       ...\n   ```\n\n5. **API Rate Limiting** (REQ-51):\n   ❌ REJECT: High-traffic endpoints without rate limiting\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Redis-based rate limiting (100 req/min per user)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Stricter limits for authentication (5 failed attempts)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: DDoS protection (IP-based blocking)\n   \n   Example violations:\n   ```python\n   # BAD - No rate limiting\n   @router.post(\"/api/auth/login\")\n   async def login(credentials: LoginRequest):\n       ...\n   \n   # GOOD - Rate limited\n   @router.post(\"/api/auth/login\")\n   @rate_limit(max_attempts=5, window=300)  # 5 attempts per 5 min\n   async def login(credentials: LoginRequest):\n       ...\n   ```\n\n6. **Input Validation** (REQ-45.5):\n   ❌ REJECT: Accepting user input without validation\n   ❌ REJECT: File uploads without type/size checks\n   ❌ REJECT: Email/phone without regex validation\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Pydantic models for API requests\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Max request size (10 MB)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Whitelist validation (allowed characters only)\n   \n   Example violations:\n   ```python\n   # BAD - No validation\n   email = request.json.get(\"email\")\n   \n   # GOOD - Pydantic validation\n   class UserCreate(BaseModel):\n       email: EmailStr  # Auto-validates email format\n       phone: constr(regex=r'^05\\d{9}$')  # Turkish mobile\n       name: constr(min_length=2, max_length=100)\n   ```\n\n7. **Sensitive Data Exposure** (REQ-45.6):\n   ❌ REJECT: Logging sensitive data (passwords, tokens, PII)\n   ❌ REJECT: Exposing stack traces in production\n   ❌ REJECT: Returning raw database errors to client\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Redacting sensitive fields in logs\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Generic error messages in production\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Separate DEBUG/PRODUCTION logging\n   \n   Example violations:\n   ```python\n   # BAD - Logging password\n   logger.info(f\"Login attempt: {email} / {password}\")\n   \n   # GOOD - Redacted\n   logger.info(f\"Login attempt: {email} / [REDACTED]\")\n   ```\n\n8. **Secure Headers** (REQ-45.7):\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS)\n   ✅ REQUIRE: X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff\n   ✅ REQUIRE: X-Frame-Options: DENY\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Content-Security-Policy\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Referrer-Policy: no-referrer\n\n9. **Dependency Vulnerabilities** (REQ-45.8):\n   ❌ REJECT: Using packages with known CVEs\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Regular dependency updates\n   ✅ REQUIRE: npm audit / pip-audit before deploy\n   ✅ REQUIRE: Pinned versions in requirements.txt/package.json\n\n10. **API Key & Secrets Management** (REQ-45.9):\n    ❌ REJECT: Hardcoded API keys in code\n    ❌ REJECT: Committing .env files\n    ✅ REQUIRE: Environment variables for secrets\n    ✅ REQUIRE: API key rotation every 90 days\n    ✅ REQUIRE: Separate keys for dev/staging/prod\n\n**OWASP Top 10 Coverage**:\n- [x] A01:2021 Broken Access Control\n- [x] A02:2021 Cryptographic Failures\n- [x] A03:2021 Injection (SQL, XSS)\n- [x] A04:2021 Insecure Design\n- [x] A05:2021 Security Misconfiguration\n- [x] A06:2021 Vulnerable Components\n- [x] A07:2021 Authentication Failures\n- [x] A08:2021 Software/Data Integrity\n- [x] A09:2021 Logging/Monitoring Failures\n- [x] A10:2021 SSRF\n\n**Output Format**:\n```\nSECURITY SCAN RESULTS:\n\nCritical Vulnerabilities: [count]\n🔴 [Vulnerability type]\n   - File: [filename:line]\n   - OWASP Category: [A01-A10]\n   - Risk: SQL injection allows full DB access\n   - Fix: Use parameterized queries\n\nHigh Severity: [count]\n🟠 [Vulnerability type]\n\nMedium/Low: [count]\n🟡 [Vulnerability type]\n\nSecurity Score: [0-100]\nRecommendation: [BLOCK COMMIT / WARN / PASS]\n```\n\n**Performance Target**: < 15 seconds\n**Block Threshold**: Any CRITICAL vulnerability"
  }
}
